  "live_records": {
    "q-103933": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103933",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Consider the region $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2y\\le x\\le 3y,\\,2\\le {4}^{xy}\\le 16\\}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u=\\frac{x}{y}$ and $v=xy.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane.",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that ${T}^{-1}(D)$ is the image of $D$ under the action of the transformation ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nLet's find the image of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane. To do that, we write the region $D$ in terms of $u$ and $v,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(D) & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2y\\le x\\le 3y,\\,2\\le {4}^{xy}\\le 16\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le \\frac{x}{y}\\le 3,\\,{2}^{1}\\le {2}^{2xy}\\le {2}^{4}\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 3,\\,1\\le 2xy\\le 4\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le xy\\le 2\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le v\\le 2\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
