    },
    "q-85306": {
      "dom_id": "step-q85306",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider the region $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le {e}^{3y}\\le 8,\\,0\\le {e}^{x/5}\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u={e}^{y}$ and $v={e}^{x}.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane.",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that ${T}^{-1}(D)$ is the image of $D$ under the action of the transformation ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nLet's find the image of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane. To do that, we write the region $D$ in terms of $u$ and $v,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(D) & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le {e}^{3y}\\le 8,\\,0\\le {e}^{x/5}\\le 2\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le {({e}^{y})}^{3}\\le 8,\\,0\\le {({e}^{x})}^{1/5}\\le 2\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,\\sqrt[3]{1}\\le \\sqrt[3]{{({e}^{y})}^{3}}\\le \\sqrt[3]{8},\\,{0}^{5}\\le {({({e}^{x})}^{1/5})}^{5}\\le {2}^{5}\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le {e}^{y}\\le 2,\\,0\\le {e}^{x}\\le 32\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 32\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
