    "q-103916": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103916",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the region $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le {x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\le 4,\\,0\\le {e}^{xy}\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u=xy$ and $v={e}^{2xy}.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane.",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that ${T}^{-1}(D)$ is the image of $D$ under the action of the transformation ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nLet's find the image of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane. To do that, we write the region $D$ in terms of $u$ and $v,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(D) & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le {x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\le 4,\\,0\\le {e}^{xy}\\le 2\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le (xy)^{2}\\le 4,\\,0\\le {({e}^{xy})}^{2}\\le {2}^{2}\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le {u}^{2}\\le 4,\\,0\\le {e}^{2xy}\\le 4\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 4\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $0\\le {x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\le 4,$ we must have $-2\\le xy\\ge 2.$ Then, $-2\\le u\\le 2$ too.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
