    "q-161088": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161088",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Consider the finite region $D$ enclosed in the first quadrant of the $xy$-plane between the curves\n\n$$\nx=3y,\\,x=7y,\\,x=\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}},\\,x=\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nA transformation $T,$ where\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nmaps a rectangular region $Δ$ with sides parallel to the $u$- and $v$-axes from the $uv$-plane onto $D$ in the $xy$-plane. Given that\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (\\,\\bbox[5pt,white,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}}\\,,\\,\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhat could be the missing expression?",
      "worked_solution": "We would like to find a rectangular region of the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v\\le d\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u(x,y)\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v(x,y)\\le d\\},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the equations of the left, right, bottom, and top sides are\n\n$$\nu(x,y)=a,\\,u(x,y)=b,\\,v(x,y)=c,\\,v(x,y)=d.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze the boundary of our region $D.$ \n\nRewriting the equations \n\n$$\nx=3y,\\,x=7y,\\,x=\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}},\\,x=\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nby moving both variables $x$ and $y$ to the left-hand side, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{y}=3,\\,\\frac{x}{y}=7,\\,x{y}^{2}=4,\\,x{y}^{2}=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we put $u(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}$ and $v(x,y)=x{y}^{2},$ we can define the transformation ${T}^{-1}$ as\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:(x,y)\\to (\\,\\frac{x}{y}\\,,\\,x{y}^{2}).\n$$\n\nTo find $T,$ we should express $x$ and $y$ in terms of $u$ and $v.$ Recall that we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u=\\frac{x}{y} \\\\ v=x{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, $x=uy.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\nv=u{y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{3}=\\frac{v}{u}\\,⟹\\,y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}$ back into $x=uy,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nx=u\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}=\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}v}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the transformation $T$ can be given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}v},\\,\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
