    "q-83638": {
      "dom_id": "step-q83638",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Let $D$ be the finite region bounded by the curve \n$({x}^{3}-y)^{4}-y=1$ and the line $y=2.$ Consider the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u={x}^{3}-y$ and $v=y.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane.",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that we are given that \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}^{3}-y=u$ and $y=v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{3}-y)^{4}-y=1\\,⟹\\,{u}^{4}-v=1\\,⟹\\,v={u}^{4}-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $y=v$ into the equation of the second curve, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2\\,⟹\\,v=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the intersections of the curves in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}v={u}^{4}-1 \\\\ v=2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}u=\\pm \\sqrt[4]{3} \\\\ v=2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm \\sqrt[4]{3},2).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14166956/assets/5a2e3fd6f3669f38834359f69e68b01a1e0d1438023418c5234d4071182f4808.png)\n\nAs a result, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}(D)=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt[4]{3}\\le u\\le \\sqrt[4]{3},\\,{u}^{4}-1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-83638-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 3,\\,{u}^{4}-2\\le v\\le 2\\}",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"352\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-sop\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c7B TEX-S1\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-texatom><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D462 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D463 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.222em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.222em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2264\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D462 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2264\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 1em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-msup space=\"2\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D462 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"